<title>MEXICO: Mexican sugar growers win 26 pct price hike - paper.</title>
<headline>Mexican sugar growers win 26 pct price hike - paper.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican sugar cane growers, threatening to stage a &quot;down machetes&quot; strike against industrialists, won a 26 percent increase in cane prices, daily Reforma said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Citing unnamed industry sources, Reforma said cane growers will be paid retroactively from the start of the 1996-1997 sugar cycle which started in November and goes through to June-July.</p>
<p>Annually, Cane growers have tough price talks with mill owners at the start of each cycle and invariably threaten to halt cane cutting, a strike action known as &quot;machetes caidos.&quot;</p>
</text>
